2741	Q0	zis249	59	3.508908	instruments_tools	The measurement instrument consist of twelve situational items scenarios to determine how effectively a person can act as a member of a team or a working group. The basis for the construction of the test was formed by current reviews of teamwork related knowledge skills and abilities. The test was deliberately developed for the broadest possible applicability in different teamwork contexts. Initial empirical findings provide evidence of a plausible two factor test structure internal consistency common to the test format and satisfactory values for construct and criterion validity.
2741	Q0	zis275	60	3.4815533	instruments_tools	The I KSWE captures the construct group potency that describes the shared expectations of members of a work group to overcome even tough impediments and eventually to achieve positive results. I KSWE displays high psychometric qualities. Substantial correlations with related team constructs are indicators for both convergent construct validity and criterion validity of the instrument. The incremental validity of the I KSWE is especially pronounced.
2741	Q0	zis207	61	3.4806316	instruments_tools	Quality of life research deals with the life contents of people and the satisfaction associated with them. This scale records the identification with the residential area and as a consequence the satisfaction of the interviewees with living conditions according to certain specified criteria e.g. child friendliness air quality traffic safety . If the assessment is negative this results in dissatisfaction. If it is positive more satisfaction with the living situation is experienced.
2741	Q0	zis64	62	3.4798267	instruments_tools	The questionnaire records the tendency towards personal ecological responsibility due to external factors. The development of the scale is based on the works of Schwartz 1977 1981 .
2741	Q0	zis342	63	3.4603248	instruments_tools	A growth mindset is a belief that personal characteristics specifically intellectual ability are malleable and can be developed by investing time and effort. Numerous studies have investigated the associations between a growth mindset and academic achievement and large intervention programs have been established to train adolescents to develop a stronger growth mindset. However methodological research on the adequacy of the measures used to assess a growth mindset is scarce. In our study we conducted one of the first comprehensive assessments of the psychometric properties of Dweck s widely used three item Growth Mindset Scale in two samples adolescents aged 14 19 years and adults aged 20 64 years . We test the comparability i.e. measurement invariance of the scale across these age groups. Furthermore using the same two samples we identified and validated a single item measure to assess growth mindset in settings with severe time constraints. Results reveal that both the three item and the single item scales have acceptable psychometric properties regarding reliability comparability and validity.
2741	Q0	zis307	64	3.4592175	instruments_tools	The epidemic related Dark Future Scale for Children eDFS K is based on the Dark Future Scale by Zaleski 1996 . It assesses children s fears about the future in specific relation to an epidemic or pandemic and the associated changes and constraints in society. In the present work the scale was related to the corona pandemic in the years 2020 2021. The likert scaled questionnaire includes four items and is designed for children between the ages of eight and twelve. The scale was first adminis tered to N 140 third and fourth grade students at several elementary schools in Lower Saxony Germany in the context of the Atempause intervention study.
2741	Q0	dbd-15	65	3.454451	instruments_tools	This guide provides a practical introduction to collecting aggregated search trend data from Google. Google Trends offers access to real time and historical search query volumes reflecting public interest and attention across various topics regions and time frames. The guide covers essential features such as selecting appropriate keywords and comparing trend indices. We focus on Google because of its overwhelming market share in many coun tries including Germany. This guide is intended for social science researchers with basic knowledge of data analysis with Python or R and an interest in leveraging online search behavior for studies of public behavior and societal patterns.
2741	Q0	zis174	66	3.4443445	instruments_tools	With five items the scale measures the development of a global personal norm for environmentally friendly behavior. The development of the scale is based on the works of Schwartz 1977 1981 .
